    "narrative": "For the May 7th slate, **Corbin Carroll** (79.72) and **James Wood** (78.42) anchor our offensive strategy as our premier high-ceiling plays. **Corbin Carroll** benefits from a steady matchup against Mitch Keller, where his dynamic platoon advantage and favorable park factors align to maximize his 5x5 utility, particularly in SB potential. Similarly, **James Wood** is in a prime position to produce from the leadoff spot; his elite xwOBA of .378 paired with an opposing xERA of 4.85 suggests a high probability of finding the base paths early, making him the highest-leverage asset in our current configuration. **Mickey Moniak** (75.75) also warrants attention as a top-tier start, as his placement in the #2 hole and a favorable park bump allow him to provide excellent ROI relative to his spot in the order.\n\nThe decision-making process for the utility spot was tight, with **Tyler Soderstrom** (67.16) securing the start over the fringe internal options due to his projected #3 spot in the order against Andrew Painter. While **Luis Campusano** (55.09) and **Kyle Karros** (54.64) fall into the marginal category, they remain in the lineup to preserve our game caps, despite lower projected floors. We are monitoring **Trevor Story** (50.93) closely; while he is currently slated at #4, the slow delivery of Griffin Jax provides a rare statistical boost to **Trevor Story**\u2019s stolen base potential, mitigating the risk of facing a pitcher with a 3.02 xERA. \n\nWe are currently navigating a depleted bench as **Josh Naylor**, **Austin Riley**, and **Jose Caballero** are either off today or out of their respective starting lineups, while **Giancarlo Stanton** remains sidelined on the IL. We continue to hold roster depth in **Seiya Suzuki**, **Brice Turang**, **Gabriel Moreno**, **Max Muncy**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Zach McKinstry**, **Alex Freeland**, **Cole Young**, and **Carson Williams** to maintain flexibility, but today\u2019s optimized lineup remains the most efficient path to gaining ground in the SB and HR categories. Exercise caution with the \"Lineup Pending\" designations for **Luis Campusano**, **Trevor Story**, and **Tyler Soderstrom**; any late-shift downward in their batting order will require an immediate reassessment of their efficiency scores.",
